(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-08-16"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-08-16","label":"2026 年 8 月 16 日","date":"2026-08-16","range":"","theme":"科技","themes":["科技"],"sources":["Economist"],"title":"Well Informed","titleZh":"应知尽知","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":7,"vocab":34,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":4,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"8.16 精读.pdf","headline":{"title":"Well Informed","titleZh":"应知尽知","source":"Economist","series":"考研那些事儿之科技系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"Putting things off exacts a hefty toll. One study published in 2013 ranked 22,053 people on a procrastination scale of one to five. Each increase of one point was associated with a drop of nearly $15,000 in annual earnings. Those who habitually engage in “self-regulatory failure”, as procrastination is also known, are more prone to delaying medical treatment. A study of 3,525 Swedish university students published in 2023 found that those who scored highly for procrastination were more likely to suffer debilitating pain.","zh":"拖延的代价十分高昂。2013年，有人发表了一项研究，他们针对22053人进行了评估，按照1至5分给拖延程度打分。研究显示，拖延程度每增加1分，年收入便会下降近15000美元。习惯性出现“自我调节失败”（又名拖延症）的人，更容易延误就医。2023年，一项3525名瑞典大学生为样本的研究发现，拖延程度较高的人遭受致残性疼痛的概率更高。"},{"index":2,"en":"It gets worse. The same Swedish study also found procrastinators more prone to anxiety, stress and loneliness. A 2025 meta-analysis, published in Frontiers in Psychiatry and covering 88 studies involving 63,323 people in 17 countries, found procrastination and its resulting erosion of self-esteem to be a predictor of future depression. How might procrastination be curbed?","zh":"不仅如此。这份瑞典的研究还发现，拖延者更容易出现焦虑、压力和孤独感。2025年，《精神病学前沿》上发表了一份荟萃分析，内容涵盖了17个国家的88项研究，共63323名参与者。分析发现拖延及其导致的自尊受损，可以作为抑郁症的预测指标。那么，如何才能遏制拖延呢？"},{"index":3,"en":"Mental exercises appear to help. One set is known as mental contrasting with implementation intentions (MCII). Popularised in a number of smartphone apps, the idea is simple: picture the benefits of achieving a goal; contrast that image with the main obstacle; and devise a tactic to overcome it. In two randomised trials reported in 2020 undergraduates were given online MCII exercises designed to reduce the delaying of bedtime, which research has linked to procrastination in general. They missed their intended bedtimes by around 38 minutes less each night than those in a control group given advice about healthy sleeping habits.","zh":"心理训练可以帮助遏制拖延症。其中，有一种方法叫做心理对照结合执行意图（MCII），现已被多款手机软件所应用。其原理非常简单：你要先想出实现目标后所能获得的好处；再将这一愿景与实现目标的主要障碍进行对照；然后制定一套克服障碍的策略。在2020年发表的两项随机试验中，一批本科生在线接受了MCII训练，旨在减少其延迟就寝行为；而既有研究表明，延迟就寝与拖延存在普遍关联。与仅接受健康睡眠习惯建议的对照组相比，接受MCII训练的学生每晚的就寝延迟时间平均减少了约38分钟。"},{"index":4,"en":"Exercise shows promise too. A Chinese trial published in March assessed procrastination in 77 male teenagers. Those randomly assigned to 12 weeks of strength training, high-intensity interval training, or a combination of the two, showed “significant reductions” in putting things off. An earlier study of 564 Chinese university students, published in 2022, found that the most physically active also procrastinated less. The researchers speculated that overcoming the stress of exertion gave them a “sense of mastery” that boosted confidence and motivation.","zh":"锻炼同样具有积极成效。今年3月，中国研究人员发表了一项实验研究，他们对77名男性青少年的拖延情况进行了评估。参与人员被随机分配进行长达12周的力量训练、高强度间歇训练或两者结合训练，结果发现，他们的拖延行为均出现了“显著减少”。2022年，另一项针对564名中国大学生的早期研究发现，身体活动最积极的学生拖延程度也最低。研究人员推测，克服运动带来的压力，能让他们产生一种“掌控感”，从而增强人的自信和动力。"},{"index":5,"en":"Then there is the question of diet and other habits. A 2024 study of Italian university students found higher procrastination among breakfast- skippers, heavy drinkers and poor sleepers. The researchers speculated that missing the energy from breakfast might hinder “motivation and ability to focus on tasks”. But the skipped breakfasts may have been a consequence of procrastination, rather than a cause: studies have yet to show convincingly that diet affects it.","zh":"此外，还需要考虑饮食以及其他生活习惯的问题。一项2024年针对意大利大学生的研究发现，不吃早餐、过量饮酒以及睡眠质量较差的人，拖延程度更高。研究人员推测，缺少早餐所提供的能量可能会妨碍“完成任务的动力和专注力”。但他们之所以不吃早餐，或许恰恰也是拖延所导致，而非拖延的原因。目前尚无研究能够令人信服地证明饮食会影响拖延行为。"},{"index":6,"en":"As for medications, none as yet targets procrastination. But an intriguing finding emerged in 2021 from an American randomised controlled trial. Adults with attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder showed significant gains in cognitive executive function, including the ability to get started on tasks, while taking the stimulant lisdexamfetamine rather than a placebo.","zh":"至于药物，目前还没有任何专门针对拖延症状的药物。不过，在2021年，一项美国随机对照试验的发现耐人寻味。患有注意缺陷多动障碍（ADHD）的成年人在服用赖右苯丙胺期间，其认知执行功能出现了显著提升，包括开始着手完成任务的能力；该药物并非安慰剂，而是兴奋剂。"},{"index":7,"en":"These days, opportunities for procrastination are greater than before. Many people work from home, out of the boss’s sight. Smartphones offer endless distractions. In one review published in 2022, each of the 18 studies assessed linked excessive smartphone use to procrastination. Scrolling often delays bedtime, too. Lack of sleep impedes executive function, leading to more failures of self-regulation. It would be helpful if the scientists involved could stop dawdling.","zh":"如今，拖延的机会比以往更多。许多人居家办公，远离老板的视线。智能手机的干扰又无穷无尽。在2022年发表的一项综述中，纳入评估的18项研究全都发现，过度使用智能手机与拖延行为存在关联。刷手机也常常会导致就寝时间延迟。睡眠不足会妨碍执行功能，进而导致更多的自我调节失败。要是研究拖延的科学家们自己也能动作快点，那就再好不过了。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"procrastinate","head":"v. /prəʊˈkræstɪneɪt/ (formal disapproving) to","definition":"delay doing sth that you should do, usually because you do","gloss":"notwanttodoit拖延；耽搁【考研大纲词汇】","example":"Most often we procrastinate when faced with something we","exampleZh":"donotwanttodo.面对不想做的事情，我们经常拖延。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"exact","head":"v. /ɪɡˈzækt/ to demand and get sth from sb 要求；索","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"取【考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"She was determined to exact a promise from him. 她决意要 他作出许诺。 adj. correct in every detail 精确的；准确的 What were his exact words? 他的原话是什么？","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"hefty","head":"adj. /ˈhefti/ large; larger than usual or expected 很大","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"的；超出一般的；可观的【考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"They sold it easily and made a hefty profit. 他们毫不费力地 卖掉了它，得到了一笔可观的利润。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"toll","head":"n. /təʊl/ the amount of damage or the number of","definition":"deaths and injuries that are caused in a particular war,","gloss":"disaster,etc.（战争、灾难等造成的）毁坏；伤亡人数【考研大纲","example":"take a heavy toll (on sb/sth)/ take its toll (on sb/sth) idiom to have a bad effect on sb/sth; to cause a lot of","exampleZh":"词汇】 The official death toll has now reached 7000. 官方公布的死 亡人数现已达7000人。 damage,deaths,suffering,etc.产生恶果；造成重大损失（或伤 亡、灾难等） The recession is taking its toll on the housing markets. 经济 衰退使住房市场遭受着重大损失。","tags":[]},{"term":"prone","head":"adj. /prəʊn/ (~ to sth/to do sth) likely to suffer from","definition":"","gloss":"sthortodosthbad易于遭受；有做（坏事）的倾向【考研大纲","example":"Tired drivers were found to be particularly prone to ignore","exampleZh":"词汇】 warningsigns.据调查，疲劳驾车时特别容易忽视警示标志。","tags":[]},{"term":"debilitate","head":"v. /dɪˈbɪlɪteɪt/ (formal) to make sb’s body or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"mindweaker（使身心）衰弱，衰竭，虚弱","exampleZh":"Chemotherapy exhausted and debilitated him. 化疗使他感 到非常疲惫虚弱。 拖延的代价十分高昂。2013年，有人发表了一项研究，他 们针对22053人进行了评估，按照1至5分给拖延程度打分。 研究显示，拖延程度每增加1分，年收入便会下降近15000美 元。习惯性出现“自我调节失败”（又名拖延症）的人，更容易 延误就医。2023年，一项3525名瑞典大学生为样本的研究发 现，拖延程度较高的人遭受致残性疼痛的概率更高。","tags":[]},{"term":"meta-analysis","head":"n. /,metəə’nælisis/ a research method that","definition":"combines the results of several related studies to produce","gloss":"betterresults元分析；荟萃分析（一种将多项独立研究结果进行","example":"The researchers performed a meta-analysis to assess the","exampleZh":"统计学合并以得出综合结论的方法） overallrisk.研究人员进行了元分析以评估整体风险。","tags":[]},{"term":"erosion","head":"n. /ɪˈrəʊʒ(ə)n/ the fact of a good quality or situation","definition":"","gloss":"being gradually lost or destroyed 削弱；逐步的破坏【考研大","example":"The survey reveals a gradual erosion of the president’s","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"curb","head":"v. /kɜːb/ to control or limit sth, especially sth bad 控制，","definition":"","gloss":"抑制，限定，约束（不好的事物）【考研大纲词汇】","example":"A range of policies have been introduced aimed at curbing SYN restrain, check, control, limit, inhibit, suppress","exampleZh":"inflation.为了抑制通货膨胀实施了一系列的政策。 不仅如此。这份瑞典的研究还发现，拖延者更容易出现焦虑、 压力和孤独感。2025年，《精神病学前沿》上发表了一份荟萃 分析，内容涵盖了17个国家的88项研究，共63323名参与者。 分析发现拖延及其导致的自尊受损，可以作为抑郁症的预测指标。 那么，如何才能遏制拖延呢？","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"contrast","head":"v. /kənˈtrɑːst/ (~ A and/with B) to compare two","definition":"","gloss":"things in order to show the differences between them 对比；","example":"It is interesting to contrast the British legal system with the n. (~ between A and B) (~ to/with sb/sth) a difference between two or more people or things that you can see clearly when they are compared or put close together; the fact of comparing two or more things in order to show the The company lost $7 million this quarter in contrast to a","exampleZh":"对照【考研大纲词汇】 Americanone.把英国的法制与美国的加以对比很有意思。 differencesbetweenthem明显的差异；对比；对照 profit of $6.2 million a year earlier. 这家公司本季度亏损了 700万元，与去年同期620万元的赢利形成了对照。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"implementation","head":"n. /ˌɪmplɪmenˈteɪʃ(ə)n/ the act of starting","definition":"","gloss":"touseaplanorsystem（计划、系统的）实施，执行【考研大","example":"Various projects for constructing new schools are under","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"picture","head":"v. /ˈpɪktʃə(r)/ (~ sb as sth) to imagine sb/sth; to","definition":"","gloss":"create an image of sb/sth in your mind 想象；设想；忆起【考","example":"We found it hard to picture him as the father of teenage","exampleZh":"研大纲词汇】 sons.我们很难想象他居然是有几个十几岁儿子的父亲了。","tags":[]},{"term":"obstacle","head":"n. /ˈɒbstəkl/ (~ to sth/to doing sth) a situation, an","definition":"event, etc. that makes it difficult for you to do or achieve","gloss":"sth障碍；阻碍；绊脚石【考研大纲词汇】","example":"A lack of qualifications can be a major obstacle to finding a SYN hindrance, barrier, hurdle, impediment, obstruction","exampleZh":"job.学历不足可能成为谋职的主要障碍。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"devise","head":"v. /dɪˈvaɪz/ to invent sth new or a new way of doing","definition":"","gloss":"sth发明；设计；想出【考研大纲词汇】","example":"A new system has been devised to control traffic in the city. SYN think up","exampleZh":"控制城市交通的新系统已经设计出来。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"tactic","head":"n. /ˈtæktɪk/ (usually pl.) the particular method you","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"usetoachievesth策略；手段；招数【考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"Confrontation is not always the best tactic. 对抗并非总是上 策。 心理训练可以帮助遏制拖延症。其中，有一种方法叫做心理 对照结合执行意图（MCII），现已被多款手机软件所应用。其原 理非常简单：你要先想出实现目标后所能获得的好处；再将这一 愿景与实现目标的主要障碍进行对照；然后制定一套克服障碍的 策略。在2020年发表的两项随机试验中，一批本科生在线接受 了MCII训练，旨在减少其延迟就寝行为；而既有研究表明，延 迟就寝与拖延存在普遍关联。与仅接受健康睡眠习惯建议的对照 组相比，接受MCII训练的学生每晚的就寝延迟时间平均减少了 约38分钟。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"assess","head":"v. /əˈses/ (~ sb/sth as sth) to make a judgement","definition":"","gloss":"about the nature or quality of sb/sth 评估，评定（性质、质","example":"The young men were assessed as either safe or unsafe","exampleZh":"量）【考研大纲词汇】 drivers.这些年轻人被评定为谨慎驾驶员和不谨慎驾驶员两类。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"assign","head":"v. /əˈsaɪn/ (~ sth to sb) (~ sb sth) to give sb sth that","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"they can use, or some work or responsibility 分配（某物）；","exampleZh":"分派，布置（工作、任务等）【考研大纲词汇】 The two large classrooms have been assigned to us. 这两间 大教室分配给了我们。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"intensity","head":"n. /ɪnˈtensəti/ the strength of something that can","definition":"","gloss":"be measured such as light, sound, etc. （光、声等的）强度","example":"The intensity of the workout increased as the session went","exampleZh":"【考研大纲词汇】 on.随着训练进行，锻炼的强度不断增加。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"interval","head":"n. /ˈɪntəvl/ a period of time between two events","definition":"","gloss":"（时间上的）间隔，间隙，间歇【考研大纲词汇】","example":"The interval between major earthquakes might be 200 at (...) intervals idiom Flaming torches were positioned at intervals along the","exampleZh":"years.大地震之间的间隔时间可能有200年。 (1)withtimebetween每隔…时间；间或；不时 Buses to the city leave at regular intervals. 开往城里的公共 汽车每隔一定时间发出一班。 (2) with spaces between 每隔…距离；间隔 terrace.走廊上间隔地插着燃烧着的火炬。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"speculate","head":"v. /ˈspekjuleɪt/ (~ about/on sth) to form an","definition":"opinion about sth without knowing all the details or facts","gloss":"推测；猜测；推断【考研大纲词汇】","example":"We can speculate that the stone circles were used in some","exampleZh":"sortofpaganceremony.我们可以推测，这些石头排成的圆圈 是用于某种异教崇拜仪式的。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"exertion","head":"n. /ɪɡˈzɜːʃn/ (also exertions [pl.]) physical or mental","definition":"","gloss":"effort; the act of making an effort 努力；尽力；费力【考研大","example":"He needed to relax after the exertions of a busy day at work.","exampleZh":"纲词汇】 他忙碌工作了一天后需要休息。 n. the use of power to make sth happen 行使；运用；施加 the exertion of force/strength/authority 使用武力；使劲；行 使权力 锻炼同样具有积极成效。今年3月，中国研究人员发表了一 项实验研究，他们对77名男性青少年的拖延情况进行了评估。 参与人员被随机分配进行长达12周的力量训练、高强度间歇训 练或两者结合训练，结果发现，他们的拖延行为均出现了“显著 减少”。2022年，另一项针对564名中国大学生的早期研究发 现，身体活动最积极的学生拖延程度也最低。研究人员推测，克 服运动带来的压力，能让他们产生一种“掌控感”，从而增强人 的自信和动力。","tags":[]},{"term":"hinder","head":"v. /ˈhɪndə(r)/ (~ sb/sth from sth/from doing sth) to","definition":"","gloss":"make it difficult for sb to do sth or sth to happen 阻碍；妨","example":"SYN hamper, impede, obstruct, inhibit, retard, thwart","exampleZh":"碍；阻挡【考研大纲词汇】 An injury was hindering him from playing his best. 受伤后 他无法发挥出最高水平。 此外，还需要考虑饮食以及其他生活习惯的问题。一项2024 年针对意大利大学生的研究发现，不吃早餐、过量饮酒以及睡眠 质量较差的人，拖延程度更高。研究人员推测，缺少早餐所提供 的能量可能会妨碍“完成任务的动力和专注力”。但他们之所以 不吃早餐，或许恰恰也是拖延所导致，而非拖延的原因。目前尚 无研究能够令人信服地证明饮食会影响拖延行为。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"intriguing","head":"adj. /ɪnˈtriːɡɪ ŋ / very interesting because of","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"being unusual or not having an obvious answer 非常有趣的；","exampleZh":"引人入胜的；神秘的【考研大纲词汇】 This intriguing book is both thoughtful and informative. 这 本引人入胜的书既有思想性又有知识性。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"deficit","head":"n. /ˈdefɪsɪt/ a lack of something that is needed 不","definition":"","gloss":"足；缺乏【考研大纲词汇】","example":"n. the amount by which money spent or owed is greater The trade balance has been in deficit for the past five years.","exampleZh":"Sleep deficit can have serious effects on health. 睡眠不足会 对健康产生严重影响。 than money earned in a particular period of time 赤字；逆 差；亏损 过去五年来贸易状况一直是逆差。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"hyperactivity","head":"n. /ˌhaɪpərækˈtɪvəti/ (of a person) the state","definition":"of having more energy than is normal, becoming excited","gloss":"easily, and being unable to stay still or think about work 多","example":"Their son has been diagnosed with a hyperactivity disorder.","exampleZh":"动亢奋，过分活跃【考研大纲词汇】 他们的儿子被诊断出患有多动症。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"cognitive","head":"adj. /ˈkɒ ɡ nətɪv/ connected with mental","definition":"","gloss":"processesofunderstanding认知的；感知的；认识的（注意重","example":"As children grow older, their cognitive processes become","exampleZh":"音）【考研大纲词汇】 sharper.随着孩子们长大，他们的认知过程也变得越来越敏锐了。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"executive","head":"adj. /ɪɡˈzekjətɪv/ relating to the management","definition":"","gloss":"and carrying out of plans, decisions, or tasks 执行的【考研","example":"She has excellent executive skills, always completing","exampleZh":"大纲词汇】 projectsontime.她有出色的执行能力，总能按时完成项目。","tags":[]},{"term":"stimulant","head":"n. /ˈstɪmjələnt/ a substance that makes you more","definition":"","gloss":"activeandenergetic兴奋剂；刺激物【考研大纲词汇】","example":"The market needs a stimulant to revive investor confidence.","exampleZh":"市场需要一剂强心针来重振投资者信心。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"lisdexamfetamine","head":"n. /ˌlɪsdeksæmˈfetəmiːn/ a prescription","definition":"medication used to treat attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) and binge-eating disorder; it is a prodrug","gloss":"","example":"that is converted into dexamphetamine in the body 赖右苯","exampleZh":"丙胺（一种处方药，用于治疗注意缺陷多动障碍和暴食症）","tags":[]},{"term":"placebo","head":"n. /pləˈsiːbəʊ/ (pl.-os) a substance that has no","definition":"physical effects, given to patients who do not need medicine but think that they do, or used when testing new","gloss":"drugs（给无实际治疗需要者的）安慰剂；（试验药物用的）无效","example":"She was only given a placebo, but she claimed she got n. something that is given to try to satisfy a person who has These small concessions have been made as a placebo to","exampleZh":"对照剂【考研大纲词汇】 better - that’s the placebo effect. 只给她服用了安慰剂，但 她说好一些了——这就是安慰剂的心理作用。 not been given the thing they really want 使人宽慰的事；安 抚话 stop the workers making further demands. 这些小让步就像 安慰剂一样，可以避免工人们提出更多的要求。 至于药物，目前还没有任何专门针对拖延症状的药物。不过， 在2021年，一项美国随机对照试验的发现耐人寻味。患有注意 缺陷多动障碍（ADHD）的成年人在服用赖右苯丙胺期间，其认 知执行功能出现了显著提升，包括开始着手完成任务的能力；该 药物并非安慰剂，而是兴奋剂。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"distraction","head":"n. /dɪˈstrækʃn/ a thing that takes your attention","definition":"","gloss":"away from what you are doing or thinking about 分散注意","example":"I find it hard to work at home because there are too many","exampleZh":"力的事；使人分心的事【考研大纲词汇】 distractions.我发觉在家里工作很难，因为使人分心的事太多。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"scroll","head":"v. /skrəʊl/ to move text on a computer screen up or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"down so that you can read different parts of it 滚屏；滚动","exampleZh":"【考研大纲词汇】 Use the arrow keys to scroll through the list of files. 用箭头 键把文件目录滚动一遍。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"impede","head":"v. /ɪmˈpiːd/ (formal) to delay or stop the progress","definition":"","gloss":"ofsth阻碍；阻止【考研大纲词汇】","example":"ANT facilitate, promote, expedite, accelerate","exampleZh":"Work on the building was impeded by severe weather. 楼 房的施工因天气恶劣而停了下来。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"dawdle","head":"v. /ˈdɔːd(ə)l/ to take a long time to do sth or go","definition":"","gloss":"somewhere拖延；磨蹭；游荡【考研大纲词汇】","example":"Eleanor will be back any moment, if she doesn’t","exampleZh":"dawdle.如果埃莉诺不磨蹭，她马上就会回来了。 如今，拖延的机会比以往更多。许多人居家办公，远离老板 的视线。智能手机的干扰又无穷无尽。在2022年发表的一项综 述中，纳入评估的18项研究全都发现，过度使用智能手机与拖 延行为存在关联。刷手机也常常会导致就寝时间延迟。睡眠不足 会妨碍执行功能，进而导致更多的自我调节失败。要是研究拖延 的科学家们自己也能动作快点，那就再好不过了。 August 8TH- 14TH ｜Science & technology 群公告学习流程精读，","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】8.16 检验题__阅读理解.docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, the 2013 study found that each one-point increase on the procrastination scale was associated with _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a longer lifespan and better overall health outcomes"},{"key":"B","text":"a decline of nearly $15,000 in annual earnings"},{"key":"C","text":"an increased likelihood of seeking prompt medical treatment"},{"key":"D","text":"a reduction in self-reported loneliness among workers"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：Each increase of one point was associated with a drop of nearly $15,000 in annual earnings.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：使用了反义干扰陷阱。原文说拖延者“更容易拖延医疗”（more prone to delaying medical treatment），说明其健康状况更差，而非“寿命更长、健康更好”。","- 选项B（正确）：Para.1 明确：拖延量表上每增加1分，年收入下降近$15,000。B 项“a decline of nearly $15,000 in annual earnings”精准对应。","- 选项C（错误）：使用了反义干扰陷阱。原文说拖延者“more prone to delaying medical treatment”（更容易拖延医疗），与 C 项“更愿意及时就医”完全相反。","- 选项D（错误）：使用了无中生有陷阱。原文从未提及拖延与“孤独感降低”的关系；相反，Para.2 说拖延者“more prone to… loneliness”（更容易孤独）。","【命题技巧】","- 同义替换：正确选项将 drop 替换为 decline，保持 nearly $15,000 不变，实现词汇级替换（L1）。","- 反义干扰：干扰项 A、C 均与原文相反，利用原文中出现的医疗、健康等词制造迷惑。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"The phrase \"sense of mastery\" (Paragraph 4) most probably refers to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a feeling of accomplishment gained from overcoming physical challenges"},{"key":"B","text":"the ability to memorise complex academic material efficiently"},{"key":"C","text":"a technique used by professional athletes to perfect their routines"},{"key":"D","text":"the desire to assert dominance over others in competitive settings"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】词仅猜测题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 4","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：The researchers speculated that overcoming the stress of exertion gave them a “sense of mastery” that boosted confidence and motivation.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：Para.4 语境：研究者推测，克服运动带来的压力后，“掌控感”会提升自信和动力。这里的“mastery”指的是克服身体挑战后获得的成就感，A 项“overcoming physical challenges”精准对应。","- 选项B（错误）：使用了偷换概念陷阱。原文讨论的是运动与拖延的关系，与“记忆学术材料”无关。","- 选项C（错误）：使用了偷换概念陷阱。“sense of mastery”是一种心理感受，而非运动员的“技术手法”。","- 选项D（错误）：使用了无中生有陷阱。原文讨论的是自我提升，与“压制他人”无关。","【命题技巧】","- 上下文线索：利用同段中的“overcoming the stress of exertion”和“boosted confidence”推断“sense of mastery”的含义——克服身体挑战后的成就感。","- 偷换概念：干扰项 B、C 将“mastery”从心理层面偷换到学术或技术层面，制造迷惑。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 that the relationship between skipping breakfast and procrastination is _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"definitively causal, with poor diet directly causing procrastination"},{"key":"B","text":"purely coincidental, with no statistical connection between the two"},{"key":"C","text":"possibly bidirectional, since procrastination itself may lead to skipped meals"},{"key":"D","text":"entirely explained by heavy drinking and poor sleep quality"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·段落推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 5","【解析】","- 原文（Para.5）：But the skipped breakfasts may have been a consequence of procrastination, rather than a cause: studies have yet to show convincingly that diet affects it.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：使用了过度推理陷阱。原文明确说“研究尚未令人信服地证明饮食影响拖延”（studies have yet to show convincingly that diet affects it），如果是“明确因果”就与原文相矛盾。","- 选项B（错误）：使用了过度推理陷阱。原文说的是“尚未令人信服地证明”，不等于“没有任何关系”——研究确实发现了两者之间的关联，只是因果方向尚不明确。","- 选项C（正确）：Para.5 明确提到“不吃早餐可能是拖延的结果而非原因”（may have been a consequence of procrastination, rather than a cause），说明因果方向可能是反向的。C 项“可能是双向的”精准概括了这一不确定性。","- 选项D（错误）：使用了以偏概全陷阱。原文确实同时提及了重饮酒和睡眠差，但说的是这些因素与拖延的关联，而非“完全解释了”不吃早餐与拖延的关系。","【命题技巧】","- 逻辑推理：正确选项需要从原文“may have been a consequence...rather than a cause”推理出因果方向可能反转，属于一步推理。","- 过度推理配合：干扰项 A 将原文“尚未证明”过度推理为“明确因果”，属于典型的过度推理。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"The author mentions the 2021 American trial on lisdexamfetamine (Paragraph 6) mainly to show that _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stimulant medications should be prescribed to all chronic procrastinators"},{"key":"B","text":"ADHD is the root cause of most procrastination behaviour in adults"},{"key":"C","text":"pharmaceutical companies should invest more in procrastination-specific drugs"},{"key":"D","text":"some medications may indirectly improve the ability to start tasks, even though none directly targets procrastination"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】例证题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 6","【解析】","- 原文（Para.6）：As for medications, none as yet targets procrastination. But an intriguing finding emerged in 2021 from an American randomised controlled trial. Adults with attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder showed significant gains in cognitive executive function, including the ability to get started on tasks.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：使用了过度推理陷阱。原文只说这项试验针对的是 ADHD 成年人，从未建议将其处方给所有拖延者。","- 选项B（错误）：使用了无中生有陷阱。原文从未说“ADHD 是拖延的根本原因”，只是说这种药物帮助 ADHD 患者提升了启动任务的能力。","- 选项C（错误）：使用了无中生有陷阱。原文从未建议制药公司加大投入。","- 选项D（正确）：Para.6 首句明确说“目前没有药物直接针对拖延”（none as yet targets procrastination），随后用 lisdexamfetamine 试验说明这种药物间接提升了“启动任务的能力”。D 项同时涵盖了这两层含义，精准对应作者的论证逻辑。","【命题技巧】","- 例证功能：例子服务于观点：虽无药直接治拖延，但某些药物可能间接帮助启动任务。答案是例子所服务的观点，而非例子本身。","- 过度推理配合：干扰项 A 将针对 ADHD 的试验结果过度延伸到所有拖延者，属于典型的过度推理。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Why Smartphones Are the Root of Modern Procrastination"},{"key":"B","text":"The Economic Costs of Delay: Procrastination and Your Salary"},{"key":"C","text":"From Mental Exercises to Medication: Science Tackles Procrastination"},{"key":"D","text":"How Swedish Universities Discovered the Cure for Laziness"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·标题概括","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.2）：How might procrastination be curbed?","- 原文（Para.3-6）：依次讨论 MCII 心理练习、体育、饮食、药物等科学干预手段。","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：使用了以偏概全陷阱。智能手机仅在 Para.7 被讨论，是加剧拖延的现代因素之一，不是全文核心。","- 选项B（错误）：使用了以偏概全陷阱。工资损失仅是 Para.1 的一个细节，文章的重点是如何缓解拖延，而非拖延的经济代价。","- 选项C（正确）：全文分为两大部分：Para.1-2 说明拖延的危害，Para.3-7 依次讨论 MCII、体育、饮食、药物和现代挑战等科学干预手段。C 项“从心理练习到药物：科学应对拖延”概括性最强。","- 选项D（错误）：使用了以偏概全陷阱。瑞典大学的研究只是引用的一个数据来源，且原文从未说“发现了懒惰的治愈方法”。","【命题技巧】","- 全文脉络：正确选项需要同时涵盖问题部分（拖延的危害）和解决方案部分（科学干预），干扰项均以偏概全。","- 标题特征：正确选项“Science Tackles”体现了文章从多角度探讨科学解决方案的结构。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】8.16检验题__完型填空.docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["Putting things off ____【11】____ a hefty toll. One study published in 2013 ranked 22,053 people on a procrastination scale of one to five. Each increase of one point was ____【12】____ with a drop of nearly $15,000 in annual earnings. Those who habitually engage in “self-regulatory failure”, as procrastination is also ____【13】____, are more prone to delaying medical treatment.","Mental exercises appear to help. The idea is ____【14】____: picture the benefits of achieving a goal; ____【15】____ that image with the main obstacle; and devise a tactic to ____【16】____ it. In two randomised trials, undergraduates given these exercises missed their intended bedtimes by around 38 minutes less each night than those in a ____【17】____ group.","Exercise shows promise too. Those randomly assigned to 12 weeks of strength training showed “significant reductions” in putting things off. The researchers ____【18】____ that overcoming the stress of exertion gave them a “sense of mastery” that ____【19】____ confidence and motivation. In one review published in 2022, each of the 18 studies assessed linked ____【20】____ smartphone use to procrastination."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"inflicts"},{"key":"B","text":"exacts"},{"key":"C","text":"avoids"},{"key":"D","text":"eliminates"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (exacts)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第1句","【解析】","[A] inflicts（造成、施加）：inflicts a toll 不如 exacts a toll 自然，inflict 多搭配 damage、pain。搭配干扰。","[B] exacts（造成、索取）：exact a toll（造成沉重代价）为固定搭配。正确答案。","[C] avoids（避免）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] eliminates（消除）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"linked"},{"key":"B","text":"confused"},{"key":"C","text":"compared"},{"key":"D","text":"associated"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (associated)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析（过去分词）·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] linked（联系）：was linked with 可用，但 be associated with 是学术研究中的标准搭配。近义干扰。","[B] confused（混淆）：be confused with 语意不符。语义场干扰。","[C] compared（比较）：be compared with 语意偏离。搭配干扰。","[D] associated（关联）：was associated with a drop（与下降相关联），是流行病学研究中的标准表达。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"known"},{"key":"B","text":"defined"},{"key":"C","text":"labeled"},{"key":"D","text":"described"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (known)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析（过去分词）·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 末句","【解析】","[A] known（称为）：as procrastination is also known，be known as 是固定搭配。正确答案。","[B] defined（定义）：be defined as 过于学术化。程度差异干扰。","[C] labeled（标注）：be labeled as 语域不符。语义场干扰。","[D] described（描述）：be described as 不如 known as 精准。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"complex"},{"key":"B","text":"novel"},{"key":"C","text":"simple"},{"key":"D","text":"controversial"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (simple)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·上下文语意","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] complex（复杂的）：方向相反，后文用三个简单步骤解释。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] novel（新颖的）：语意不符，文中强调的是简单而非新颖。语义场干扰。","[C] simple（简单的）：The idea is simple，后文 picture... contrast... devise 三个步骤清晰简洁。正确答案。","[D] controversial（有争议的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"replace"},{"key":"B","text":"combine"},{"key":"C","text":"confuse"},{"key":"D","text":"contrast"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (contrast)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] replace（替换）：replace A with B 语意不符。搭配干扰。","[B] combine（结合）：combine A with B 方向偏离。搭配干扰。","[C] confuse（混淆）：confuse A with B 语意不符。搭配干扰。","[D] contrast（对比）：contrast that image with the main obstacle，contrast with 是固定搭配。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"avoid"},{"key":"B","text":"ignore"},{"key":"C","text":"overcome"},{"key":"D","text":"accept"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (overcome)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·方向","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] avoid（避免）：方向偏离，方法的核心是克服而非回避。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] ignore（忽视）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] overcome（克服）：devise a tactic to overcome it，与 sense of mastery 呼应。正确答案。","[D] accept（接受）：方向偏离。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"control"},{"key":"B","text":"treatment"},{"key":"C","text":"test"},{"key":"D","text":"study"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (control)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 末句","【解析】","[A] control（对照）：control group（对照组）是实验设计的标准术语。正确答案。","[B] treatment（实验组）：treatment group 是接受干预的组，但文中被比较的应该是未接受干预的对照组。语义场干扰。","[C] test（测试）：test group 非标准术语。语义场干扰。","[D] study（研究）：study group 非此语境的标准搭配。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"confirmed"},{"key":"B","text":"proved"},{"key":"C","text":"denied"},{"key":"D","text":"speculated"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (speculated)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·引述动词分析","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] confirmed（证实）：语气过于确定。程度差异干扰。","[B] proved（证明）：同上。程度差异干扰。","[C] denied（否认）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] speculated（推测）：The researchers speculated that，speculate 表示提出推测性假说。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"undermined"},{"key":"B","text":"boosted"},{"key":"C","text":"reduced"},{"key":"D","text":"questioned"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (boosted)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·方向","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] undermined（削弱）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] boosted（增强、提升）：boosted confidence and motivation，与 sense of mastery 的正面效果一致。正确答案。","[C] reduced（降低）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] questioned（质疑）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"moderate"},{"key":"B","text":"limited"},{"key":"C","text":"excessive"},{"key":"D","text":"occasional"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (excessive)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·感情色彩","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 末句","【解析】","[A] moderate（适度的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] limited（有限的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] excessive（过度的）：linked excessive smartphone use to procrastination，与全文拖延有害的主题一致。正确答案。","[D] occasional（偶尔的）：方向相反。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"8.16 精读.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":731452,"date":"2026-08-16","range":"","title":"Well Informed","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.16 精读.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.16 检验题__阅读理解.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":55407,"date":"2026-08-16","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.16 检验题__阅读理解.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.16检验题__完型填空.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":58279,"date":"2026-08-16","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.16检验题__完型填空.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"8.16杂志排版.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":754465,"date":"2026-08-16","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.16杂志排版.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
